{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/pingora/pulls/1117","id":5213501083,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJfWe5M8AAAABNr-2mw","html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/pingora/pull/1117","diff_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/pingora/pull/1117.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/pingora/pull/1117.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/pingora/issues/1117","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/pingora/pulls/1117/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/pingora/pulls/1117/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/pingora/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/pingora/issues/1117/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/pingora/statuses/522eb28e4b2dba6449274ed7267edca0b8137184","number":1117,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"refactor(core): replace the unmaintained serde_yaml with serde-saphyr (RUSTSEC-2024-0449)","user":{"login":"lopatnov","id":11029246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDI5MjQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11029246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov","html_url":"https://github.com/lopatnov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Refs #779 (replace the deprecated `serde_yaml`; the maintainers' answer there was that they would). Fixes #1058 (RUSTSEC-2024-0449).\n\n## Why\n\n`serde_yaml` is archived, and it pulls in `unsafe-libyaml`, which the advisory RUSTSEC-2024-0449 reports as unmaintained. It reaches every downstream project through `pingora-core`, so each of them has to ignore the advisory (#1058). `serde-saphyr` is safe Rust, maintained, and the replacement the advisory suggests.\n\n## What\n\n- `pingora-core`: `ServerConf::from_yaml` and `ServerConf::to_yaml` use `serde_saphyr::from_str` / `to_string`. The API of `pingora-core` does not change.\n- `pingora-proxy`: the `modify_response` example (and the dev-dependency) uses `serde_saphyr::to_string`.\n- The one test that inspected a `serde_yaml::Value` (`test_working_directory_deserializes_from_yaml_string`) now checks the written yaml and that it reads back as the same configuration.\n- A second commit changes the CI toolchain matrix (see below).\n\n`serde_yaml` and `unsafe-libyaml` are gone from the dependency tree of `pingora-core` and `pingora-proxy` (`cargo tree -i unsafe-libyaml` finds nothing).\n\n## The MSRV (please read)\n\n`serde-saphyr` uses let chains and declares `rust-version = \"1.89\"` (its releases from 1.2.0 on; 1.1.0 declares nothing but already fails on 1.85 with `error[E0658]: let expressions in this position are unstable`). The job that checks the oldest toolchain, 1.85.0, therefore cannot build `pingora-core` with it. This was the question raised in #779 (\"it requires rust 1.89\").\n\nI kept that change in its own commit, so it is easy to drop or rework: the oldest toolchain in `.github/workflows/build.yml` becomes `1.89.0` (same exclusions as before), and `pingora-cache`, which declares a `rust-version` and depends on `pingora-core`, declares `1.89`. I did not touch `clippy.toml` (`msrv = \"1.85\"`), because changing it can enable new lints, which is a separate decision. If you prefer to keep 1.85, the alternative is a maintained fork of the same libyaml port (for example `serde_norway`), which keeps the C-translated parser and may build on 1.85; I did not try it. Tell me which way you prefer and I will rework the PR.\n\n## Checked\n\n- `cargo test -p pingora-core --lib server::configuration`: 14 passed, on stable (1.99.1, Linux).\n- `cargo check -p pingora-core -p pingora-proxy -p pingora-cache -p pingora-load-balancing --all-targets` and `cargo check -p pingora-proxy --example modify_response` on 1.89.0 and on stable.\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` is clean.\n- Not run here: `cargo check --workspace` (the BoringSSL crates need libclang, which my machine lacks), the TLS-backend tests, the 1.89.0 test leg of CI.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T17:32:31Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T17:32:31Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"lopatnov:replace-serde-yaml-with-serde-saphyr","ref":"replace-serde-yaml-with-serde-saphyr","repo":{"id":1450490589,"node_id":"R_kgDOVnS63Q","name":"pingora","full_name":"lopatnov/pingora","owner":{"login":"lopatnov","id":11029246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDI5MjQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11029246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov","html_url":"https://github.com/lopatnov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lopatnov/events